1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,414
When selvage uses smart context, it sends the model only the code blocks that contain changed lines.

2
00:00:07,414 --> 00:00:12,381
For that it first needs the range of lines a hunk actually changed.

3
00:00:12,381 --> 00:00:16,755
Let us follow the function that computes it, in a debugger.

4
00:00:16,755 --> 00:00:23,204
The input is one hunk from the repository test, and the modified file starts at line 1.

5
00:00:23,204 --> 00:00:26,096
First, the content is split into lines.

6
00:00:26,096 --> 00:00:27,282
There are seven.

7
00:00:27,282 --> 00:00:31,285
Next, a tracker is created with current_line set to 1.

8
00:00:31,285 --> 00:00:33,880
Now the lines are taken one by one.

9
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:38,904
The first line starts with a space, so it is a context line.

10
00:00:38,904 --> 00:00:43,033
The branch passes ADDED and DELETED and reaches CONTEXT.

11
00:00:43,033 --> 00:00:49,374
A context line also exists in the modified file, so only current_line moves up by one.

12
00:00:49,374 --> 00:00:52,913
The second context line is handled the same way.

13
00:00:52,913 --> 00:00:56,600
So when the third line arrives, current_line is 3.

14
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:01,011
The third line, 'old line', starts with a minus sign.

15
00:01:01,011 --> 00:01:04,104
An empty line would return None right away.

16
00:01:04,104 --> 00:01:07,627
Otherwise the first character is taken as prefix.

17
00:01:07,627 --> 00:01:11,511
Then the loop compares it with each LineType in order.

18
00:01:11,511 --> 00:01:13,884
ADDED's plus sign does not match.

19
00:01:13,884 --> 00:01:16,976
The second one, DELETED's minus sign, does.

20
00:01:16,976 --> 00:01:19,278
On a match the type is returned.

21
00:01:19,278 --> 00:01:23,880
A line that matches no sign becomes None, and the loop skips it.

22
00:01:24,480 --> 00:01:27,298
DELETED goes to _process_deleted_line.

23
00:01:27,298 --> 00:01:33,378
No change has been recorded yet, so first_change_line becomes the current line, 3.

24
00:01:33,378 --> 00:01:37,530
last_change_line is also empty, so it becomes 3 as well.

25
00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:44,055
And current_line stays at 3, because a deleted line does not exist in the modified file.

26
00:01:44,055 --> 00:01:48,800
The deletion is marked at line 3, where the next line will land.

27
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:54,376
The next two lines start with a plus sign; they are added lines.

28
00:01:54,376 --> 00:01:57,796
first_change_line is already 3, so it stays.

29
00:01:57,796 --> 00:02:01,450
last_change_line is set to the current line, 3.

30
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:07,670
An added line really exists in the modified file, so current_line moves up to 4.

31
00:02:07,670 --> 00:02:14,200
On the second added line, last_change_line becomes 4 and current_line moves up to 5.

32
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:19,521
The two remaining context lines only move current_line up to 7.

33
00:02:19,521 --> 00:02:22,743
When the loop ends, the range is finalized.

34
00:02:22,743 --> 00:02:27,165
The recorded first change, 3, and last change, 4, are read.

35
00:02:27,165 --> 00:02:33,609
Without a record it would fall back to the start line, and anything below 1 becomes 1.

36
00:02:33,609 --> 00:02:35,632
The result is lines 3 to 4.

37
00:02:35,632 --> 00:02:39,079
That matches what the repository test expects.

38
00:02:39,079 --> 00:02:44,400
selvage then picks the code blocks around this range as review context.
